# SRG-APP-000097-AU-000700  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must produce audit records containing information
# to establish where the events occurred.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000097-AU-000700
group:           V-221910
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000132
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk stamps host, source, sourcetype and index on every record it
                 indexes. The application assigns the destination index and the sourcetype
                 per data input, and derives the host either statically (inputs.conf host)
                 or from the path of the file being read (host_regex, host_segment), so
                 each record states where it came from and where it is held.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [<input stanza>] index non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [<input stanza>] sourcetype non_empty

external:        For records arriving over the network the origin is resolved by
                 inputs.conf connection_host, assessed under SRG-APP-000098-AU-000710, and
                 reverse lookups there depend on the DNS service.
external:        The sending host must identify itself in the record or in the
                 Splunk-to-Splunk header; Splunk cannot reconstruct an origin the sender
                 withheld.
external:        Where host_regex or host_segment derives the host from a path, the naming
                 convention of that path is a property of the sending system.

citation:        SRG-APP-000097-AU-000700 check text; SPLK-CL-000110 fix text;
                 inputs.conf.spec:60 (host = <string>), :93-96 (index = <string>), :113-116
                 (sourcetype = <string>), :244-262 (host_regex = <regular expression>,
                 host_segment = <integer>)
finding:         Data inputs in inputs.conf do not assign the destination index and
                 sourcetype, so the records Splunk Enterprise produces do not establish
                 where the event occurred or where it is held.
